This adds the freebsd-port skill. The first patch is your spec.org
from the claude-skill-freebsd-port bookmark, unchanged, so the series
applies to trunk on its own. The second adds SKILL.md, which turns
the spec into steps Claude can run in lab-claude.

SKILL.md settles the points the spec leaves open, so they live in the
tree rather than on the list:

- The tree is a blobless git clone at /var/tmp/freebsd-ports. Each run
  fetches, discards whatever an earlier run left, and branches from
  origin/main.
- "Getting metadata" covers fetch, makesum, extract (to read
  upstream's dependency lists and tests), and helper targets such as
  cargo-crates. Configure, build, stage, and check-plist are out, so
  the plist is drafted and marked unverified in the patch notes.
- "All the linters" means portclippy, portfmt -D (a diff to apply by
  hand, never a rewrite in place), and portlint -A. The skill stops if
  any is missing.
- Patches go To you and Cc lab-devel, made with plain git
  format-patch and the "freebsd-ports PATCH" prefix.
- Commit messages follow oss/freebsd-ports/CLAUDE.md, without the PR:
  trailer, since no bug exists yet.
- An update to a port that is already at the latest good version
  stops without posting anything.

Testing: I cloned the tree into /var/tmp and ran the update steps and
the portmake wrapper against it. makesum and extract on sysutils/tree
work as written. cargo-crates works on textproc/ripgrep. The tree stays
clean afterwards. Without PORT_DBDIR and BATCH, extract fails in the
config step trying to su to create /var/db/ports. I could not run the
lint step, because portclippy, portfmt, and portlint are still not
installed in lab-claude. I have not run the whole skill on a real
port yet.

